  "releaseNotes": "Conformance correctness across serialization, FunctX/spec functions, collation, numeric and derived-integer operations, and date arithmetic. Serialization gains the full set of output methods (adaptive, xml, json, text, html, xhtml) with correct per-method options. Derived integer types compare and hash by value in distinct-values/group-by/deep-equal. map:merge single-arg use-first is O(1) per entry. date/dateTime +/- duration now computes on the proleptic Gregorian calendar across the year-1 boundary (requires PhoenixmlDb.Core 1.2.0). Backward-compatible; no public API removed. See RELEASES.md for full notes.",
